* ============================================================================
*  LOAD_CC - constant-current electronic load for simulation
*  Draws I amps from P to N once enabled at TON (ramped over TRISE).
*  Unlike an ideal current source it folds back below VMIN, so it cannot
*  force the node to impossible voltages when the BMS opens the FETs.
*  CIN models the load's input (bulk) capacitance - a real motor controller
*  has hundreds of uF - and keeps FET switching events solvable.
*    P, N   load terminals (current flows into P, out of N)
*    I      load current, A          TON    turn-on time, s
*    TRISE  ramp time, s             VMIN   fold-back voltage, V
*    CIN    load input capacitance, F (default 10u)
*    RESR   series resistance of CIN incl. wiring, ohm (default 0.1) -
*           limits the inrush when the DSG FET closes onto the load
* ============================================================================
.subckt LOAD_CC P N params: I=1 TON=0 TRISE=1m VMIN=20 CIN=10u RESR=0.1
Ven en 0 PWL(0 0 {TON+1u} 0 {TON+1u+TRISE} 1)
Bld P N I = ({I})*V(en)*min(1, max(0, V(P,N)/({VMIN})))
Cin P pc {CIN}
Resr pc N {RESR}
Rpn P N 100Meg
.ends LOAD_CC

* ============================================================================
*  SIM_PROBE - one-pin probe for a test-point symbol. Put a global label on
*  its pin (e.g. PACK_SOC, PACK_AH_OUT, PACK_TEMP, BMS_AH_OUT, BMS_SOC) and
*  click the wire in the simulator to plot that quantity. 1e12 ohm to ground,
*  so it does not load anything.
* ============================================================================
.subckt SIM_PROBE P
Rp P 0 1e12
.ends SIM_PROBE
